// pfodWeb NOTE: excludes GPIO4/33 (Teleinfo/TIC reader enable+RX),
// GPIO8 (TIC RX on 2nd-revision PICOV3 board), GPIO14 (LoRa reset),
// GPIO26/27 (LoRa TX/RX on 1st revision, ambiguous with LED on 2nd) -
// see vendor pins_arduino.h.
// pfodWeb NOTE (2026-07-14 correction): also excludes GPIO25 - this pin
// is dedicated onboard RGB LED hardware on BOTH board revisions, missed
// by the earlier pass: RGB_LED_PIN (single-wire addressable LED data
// line) on the 1st-revision ARDUINO_DENKY_WROOM32, and LED_BLU_PIN (blue
// channel of a 3-pin RGB LED, alongside GPIO26/27) on the 2nd-revision
// ARDUINO_DENKY_PICOV3. Since both physical variants dedicate this pin
// to onboard LED hardware (never general-purpose), and the exact
// capability needed differs by revision (addressable-LED vs
// discrete-channel), it is excluded rather than guessed - same
// never-guess policy already applied to GPIO26/27 above. Confirmed via
// this board's own vendor pins_arduino.h (which is itself sourced
// directly from the real board designer's own upstream contribution -
// see notes.txt for the GitHub PR citation).
